# Ensemble.ReaperOSC
# OSC pattern config file for the ensemble-reaper bridge.
#
# Install: copy this file into %APPDATA%\REAPER\OSC\ (open it from the OSC
# control surface settings dialog via "open config directory"), then select
# it as the pattern config for the bridge's OSC device.
#
# Derived from Default.ReaperOSC with:
# - Larger banks (64 tracks, 16 FX slots, 64 parameters each) to cover real
#   sessions. Adjust here if you need more.
# - Only the patterns the bridge models. Track-scoped (@) patterns only, so
#   every track reports rather than just the device-selected one.
# - Flood-prone feedback removed: VU, SAMPLES, FRAMES, TIME/BEAT string
#   variants. BEAT is kept as a raw float (it feeds the bridge's position
#   Stream) — comment it out if you don't want position at all.
#
# See the comments in Default.ReaperOSC for the full pattern syntax.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------

DEVICE_TRACK_COUNT 64
DEVICE_SEND_COUNT 4
DEVICE_RECEIVE_COUNT 4
DEVICE_FX_COUNT 16
DEVICE_FX_PARAM_COUNT 64
DEVICE_FX_INST_PARAM_COUNT 64
DEVICE_MARKER_COUNT 0
DEVICE_REGION_COUNT 0

REAPER_TRACK_FOLLOWS REAPER
DEVICE_TRACK_FOLLOWS DEVICE
DEVICE_TRACK_BANK_FOLLOWS DEVICE
DEVICE_FX_FOLLOWS DEVICE

DEVICE_EQ INSERT
DEVICE_ROTARY_CENTER 0

# ----------------------------------------------------------------

# Transport
PLAY t/play
STOP t/stop
PAUSE t/pause
RECORD t/record
REWIND b/rewind

# Tempo and playhead position
TEMPO f/tempo/raw
TIME f/position/seconds
BEAT f/position/beat

# Master
MASTER_VOLUME n/master/volume

# Tracks (track-scoped only — the bridge addresses tracks explicitly)
TRACK_NAME s/track/@/name
TRACK_VOLUME n/track/@/volume
TRACK_PAN n/track/@/pan
TRACK_MUTE b/track/@/mute
TRACK_SOLO b/track/@/solo
TRACK_REC_ARM b/track/@/recarm

# FX (track-scoped only — feedback flows for all tracks)
FX_NAME s/track/@/fx/@/name
FX_BYPASS b/track/@/fx/@/bypass
FX_PARAM_NAME s/track/@/fx/@/fxparam/@/name
FX_PARAM_VALUE n/track/@/fx/@/fxparam/@/value

# Escape hatch: trigger any REAPER action by command ID
ACTION i/action t/action/@
